{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/850658-pugmire-new-trick-apprentice-mage","id":850658,"title":"[Pugmire] New [Trick] - Apprentice Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-21T10:27:05-07:00","id":850658,"title":"[Pugmire] New [Trick] - Apprentice Mage","content":"I think this is a common archetype for rogue-type characters, I was thinking about how Pathfinder implemented it, and of course, Pugmire explicitly references Fafhrd and the Gray Mouser as one of the inspirations for the setting. So here's an idea for a Ratter trick that will hopefully be balanced against Pugmire's expectations and provide a little of that flavor.<br /> <br /> <b>Apprentice Mage</b><br /> The ratter has picked up a few arcane tricks. <br /> The ratter doubles her aptitude bonus on all Know Arcana checks.<br /> <br /> <i>Refinements</i><br /> - The ratter may choose a single 0-level spell from the Artisan list. The ratter may use this spell as a spell-like ability once per day, at a caster level equal to her ratter level.<br /> - The ratter may choose a single 1st-level spell from the Artisan list. The ratter may use this spell as a spell-like ability once per day, at a caster level equal to her ratter level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11291-tim4488","name":"Tim4488","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}